{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "init:i1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process"
      ],
      "justification": "Start node maps directly to the introductory phrase."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_ret->n2",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the first XOR decision and captures the customer return path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_ret->n3",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the alternative crew pickup path and the reconvergence point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly models the counting and comparison action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_status->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the order status check and models the complete/returned path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_status->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the incomplete/missing items path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_status->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the damaged item path (including the email action) and reconvergence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_dest1->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "First destination decision and the packing path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_dest1->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Alternative storing path and reconvergence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_post->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Post-processing branch opening and the missing-items email path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_post->n11",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Damaged items inventory removal path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_post->n_proc",
        "action:n_proc"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Reuses the complete-order condition to model the explicit 'proceed' continuation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_cust->n12",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Follow-up decision on missing items and the positive return path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_cust->n13",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Negative return path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit termination point modeled as an end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_repair->n15",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Repair decision branch and the successful repair path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_repair->n16",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Discard path, associated email action, and convergence point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_dest2->n17",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Second destination decision and packing path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_dest2->n18",
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Alternative storing path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Second explicit termination point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The customer is then emailed with replacement charges, and the process is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Final email action and third termination point capturing process completion."
    }
  ],
